# What belongs to the workshop, not to the program.
#
# The source archive GitHub builds from a branch or a tag is what people
# download and what an update installs, so it should hold TrackImage and
# nothing else. These are for whoever works on it: the automation, the notes
# for Claude, the ignore list. Useful in a clone, noise in an installation --
# somebody unpacking the ZIP should not have to wonder what CLAUDE.md is or
# whether they are allowed to delete it.
#
# export-ignore is honoured by `git archive`, which is what GitHub's
# "Source code (zip)" is made with. Nothing here affects a clone, and the
# workflow still runs: Actions checks the repository out, it does not unpack
# an archive.
/.github         export-ignore
/.gitattributes  export-ignore
/.gitignore      export-ignore
/CLAUDE.md       export-ignore
